# Error Handling

## Error Classification

Always classify errors appropriately:

```python
# ✅ GOOD
class ValidationError(Exception):
    """Data validation failed - don't retry"""
    pass

class DatabaseError(Exception):
    """Database operation failed - retry"""
    pass

class ExternalAPIError(Exception):
    """External service failed - retry with backoff"""
    pass

class FatalError(Exception):
    """Unrecoverable error - send to DLQ"""
    pass
```

## Error Handling Pattern

```python
# ❌ BAD
try:
    process()
except Exception as e:
    print(f"Error: {e}")

# ✅ GOOD
try:
    await process()
except ValidationError as e:
    logger.warning(f"Validation failed: {e}")
    await dlq.send(message)
except DatabaseError as e:
    logger.error(f"Database error: {e}")
    if retry_count < MAX_RETRIES:
        await retry_with_backoff(message)
    else:
        await dlq.send(message)
except FatalError as e:
    logger.critical(f"Fatal error: {e}")
    await dlq.send(message)
```

## Logging Errors

Always log errors with context:

```python
# ✅ GOOD
logger.error(
    "Failed to process message",
    extra={
        "message_id": message["id"],
        "event_type": message["type"],
        "error": str(e),
        "retry_count": retry_count
    }
)
```
